    {
      "id": "DyksVovJg5lKkBJBozpak",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1591.344301991699,
      "y": 835.0561234221266,
      "width": 1662.4073688279868,
      "height": 885.624952445081,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 30498014,
      "version": 130,
      "versionNonce": 1042770434,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784699875062,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key points: \n\n(Refer:  https://www.perplexity.ai/search/5f177d8b-22f5-47fd-84dd-\ndff1a6bafd4f)\n\nProducer produces data to a topic. The message can go to any partition of the\ntopic(different algo like round robin, etc).\nProducer doesnt know which consumer will read data\nProducer can also produce to a specific partition(by giving partition key)  of a\ntopic.\nconsumers of a consumer group consumes from a topic. \neach cosumer from a consumer group can listen to only only 1 partition of the\ntopic\n1 consumer can read/listen from 2 partiton present in 2 different topic.\ntwo consumer form 2 same consumer group cannot listen from same partition\ntwo consumer form 2 different consumer group can listen from same partition\n1 consumer group is like 1 service.",
      "fontSize": 41.67646835035676,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key points: \n\n(Refer:  https://www.perplexity.ai/search/5f177d8b-22f5-47fd-84dd-dff1a6bafd4f)\n\nProducer produces data to a topic. The message can go to any partition of the topic(different algo like round robin, etc).\nProducer doesnt know which consumer will read data\nProducer can also produce to a specific partition(by giving partition key)  of a topic.\nconsumers of a consumer group consumes from a topic. \neach cosumer from a consumer group can listen to only only 1 partition of the topic\n1 consumer can read/listen from 2 partiton present in 2 different topic.\ntwo consumer form 2 same consumer group cannot listen from same partition\ntwo consumer form 2 different consumer group can listen from same partition\n1 consumer group is like 1 service.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "MCwLA4vMrw5_dTM4MNgFC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 531.1634476106573,
      "y": 3481.236868650294,
      "width": 1759.7708740234375,
      "height": 1155,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1278267714,
      "version": 1371,
      "versionNonce": 1425268290,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "qNCj30FDK5w78QxJmW-NO",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1784711262353,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Interview Questions\n\na kakfa topic \"Order topic\" has 6 partitions.\n\nIf there are \n6 consumers:  consumer points to 1 partition (happy path)\n2 consumer:  each of these 3 consumer point to 3 partitions\n4 consumer:  6 partitions are divided amoung 4 consumer(some consumer may point to 2 partition)\n8 consumer: 6 consumers point to 6 partition and the remaining 2 consumers are idle\n\nkafka internally uses soemthing called \"consumer rebalancing\" technique to re-assign the partiiton to the consumes.\n\nIf a consumer dies/crashed. then rebalancing happens and new consumer is assign to partition.\nConsumer rebalanicng happens at conusmer roup level not at single consumer instance level.\n\n** during rebalancing, all consumers pause for a while, rebalancing happens and then all consumers start up - Traditional kafka\n** In Mordern Kafka we have \"co-operative rebalancing\",\n\n\nHowmany copies of kafka messages are stored in kafka? depends on replication factor => if 3\nleader copy:1\nfollowers copy : 2\n\n\n\nhow does kafka gurantee ordering? \nkafka does do it internally.\nbut while sending messages we attach a key . and all the messages assocaited with that key goes to a particular partition only.\n\n\nusing \"offset\" ay consumer group level\n\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Interview Questions\n\na kakfa topic \"Order topic\" has 6 partitions.\n\nIf there are \n6 consumers:  consumer points to 1 partition (happy path)\n2 consumer:  each of these 3 consumer point to 3 partitions\n4 consumer:  6 partitions are divided amoung 4 consumer(some consumer may point to 2 partition)\n8 consumer: 6 consumers point to 6 partition and the remaining 2 consumers are idle\n\nkafka internally uses soemthing called \"consumer rebalancing\" technique to re-assign the partiiton to the consumes.\n\nIf a consumer dies/crashed. then rebalancing happens and new consumer is assign to partition.\nConsumer rebalanicng happens at conusmer roup level not at single consumer instance level.\n\n** during rebalancing, all consumers pause for a while, rebalancing happens and then all consumers start up - Traditional kafka\n** In Mordern Kafka we have \"co-operative rebalancing\",\n\n\nHowmany copies of kafka messages are stored in kafka? depends on replication factor => if 3\nleader copy:1\nfollowers copy : 2\n\n\n\nhow does kafka gurantee ordering? \nkafka does do it internally.\nbut while sending messages we attach a key . and all the messages assocaited with that key goes to a particular partition only.\n\n\nusing \"offset\" ay consumer group level\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
